  "salt": "_yCsOUpQUHpSWY6LWdDZZw==",
  "text": "A killeen is an Irish sacred place. Across Ireland, children's burial grounds called killeens are found, marked on maps and preserved. These small fields or groves held the remains of fetuses that were miscarried and babies who died without Christian baptism. Such children could not be buried in Christian cemeteries. Their parents laid them to rest in ground sacred before Christianity reached Ireland. Few of the deities these grounds first served are remembered.",
